WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701
-I want talk about something
you write about your book.

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
You write about your passion
for picking up garbage.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, because we live in --
I live in England now.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I didn't notice it

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.078 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in London so much,

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:15.181
but then we moved to West Sussex
in a little village.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:19.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's in
the South Downs National Park.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so the downs are like
these massive hills

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are so green
they make your eyes ache.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we live on a, you know,
a narrow one-lane road.

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:28.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so if two cars are coming,
one has to pull off.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like, a cottage
that looks like a storybook.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
But people throw everything
out the car window.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everything. You finished with
that newspaper?

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.070 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Throw it out the window.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
Coffee cup? Throw it out
the window.

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:39.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sandwich?
Throw it out the window.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.975 size:84% position:42%
And when I moved there,
I wrote -- and I said,

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:45.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Is there a parade?"
Like, I couldn't conceive.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:49.349 line:92%
And every...So I had a meeting

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
and was proposing
a bunch of things,

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they said,
"No, we can't. No, we can't."

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I just thought,
"Okay fine, I'll do it."

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:56.723 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.958 size:75% position:38%
So it's -- it's like
an 8-hour a day job.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:02.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And I have an outfit,

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:05.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I pick up trash
for eight hours a day.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:10.070
-And you've written that
it's actually not that bad.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
You listen to a podcast.
You listen to...

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I just think of it as my job.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:17.544
But people see me, and they just
think that I'm crazy.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:18.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, they...
-Yeah.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:22.415
-If I come upon a family,
they pull their children close.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
They...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.086 line:92%
-Yeah, because usually, people,

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
in order to do what
you're doing,

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
have had
to have committed a crime.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Right.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:34.561
No, a lot of people think
that I'm a felon and...

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a grabber.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:39.365
-And I have...I mean, when I
say I have an outfit, like,

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:42.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
they want me to wear
this reflector, but I'm not.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:43.336 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's more like
a hobo outfit that I wear.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:45.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like with big patches,
like a Broadway --

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
if there was a Broadway play
called "Hobo,"

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:50.844 line:92%
that's what I'm dressed like.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:53.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But now, this has not
gone unnoticed.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
They actually --
I guess the town --

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:57.717
is it the town that gave you --
bestowed this honor?

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:01.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
They named a garbage truck
after you.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:03.823 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-This is true.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is the Pig Pen Sedaris
garbage truck.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Well, because...

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:11.464 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:12.932 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Well...

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
they were gonna put my name
on it, and I thought,

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.937
"Well, 'Sedaris' on a garbage
truck just wouldn't make sense."

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't really have
a nickname.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:20.473 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I always wanted one.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.975 size:75% position:38%
And you can't really
give yourself one.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:25.411
So I thought, "Okay, Pig Pen,"
so it'd just have pig on it...

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...and then make it

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.614 size:78% position:39%
a little bit better.
-These -- By the way,

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
these couldn't look
more like what I pictured

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.317
British women who come
to this kind of ceremony.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Everything.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The local paper
did an article about it.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:38.625
The article was just like,
"Local man picks up trash."

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And then someone in America

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
saw it and said,
"Don't you know who this is?"

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:44.063 size:88% position:44%
And so they rewrote it.
But it doesn't matter...

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...that I'm an author.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn't really matter.
-No, that's not what

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:47.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is about.
-No.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have to ask,
in your trash picking up,

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:53.173
have you seen that newspaper
article on the ground yet?

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:56.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:56.843 line:92%
'Cause that would really --

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's, like,
circle of life right there.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:03.216
You actually were invited to
speak to the House of Commons

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
based on
your trash proclivities.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:07.253
-I went and I testified to the
House of Commons about litter.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What did you testify about?
Just litter?

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:12.425
-Well, it was me and the head
of the tobacco manufacturers,

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a guy --
a woman who owns, like,

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:15.595 line:92%
eight McDonald's franchises.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:18.798
And when it was my turn, I just
said, "I'm not -- I'm nobody.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:21.568
"I just pick up rubbish,
and here's what I pick up

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:22.335 line:92%
and here's what I notice."

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:25.838
But it never occurred to me that
anyone would be for litter.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:29.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-But one of the MPs was just,

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:32.245 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"So, Mr. Se-dah-ris..."

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like -- Oh, maybe he said,
"Mr. Se-dah-ris,"

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:38.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
as if, like,
that's not really my name.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:41.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You live in Horsham,
a very wealthy...

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:43.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
"[ Clears throat ]
part of the country.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.924 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"So tell me, sir,

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:47.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
"is somebody throwing a can
out their car window

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
the biggest problem
you have down there?"

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:52.332
And I'm just not used to being
talked to that way, you know?

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-And I was just flustered.

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:55.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
But for the rest of my life,
I'll resent saying --

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll be mad at myself
for not saying, "Oh, God, no.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:03:59.906 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"No, no, no.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
The biggest problem
is your mother's whoring."

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:05.812 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:07.280 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What would they...

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:10.750 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Cheering ]

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
what would they --
what would they do?

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
they couldn't imprison you.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:16.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I think if
you said that,

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.625
you'd be back in the newspaper.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:20.126 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-But who's for trash?

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:22.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, who's for litter?
-Who is for it?

